  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) All group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> elements form oxides of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> type where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>o</mi></math>. And these oxides produces acids on hydrolysis.</p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is reducing while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is an oxidising agent. An oxidising agent is a substance that causes oxidation by accepting electrons; therefore, it gets reduced. A reducing agent is a substance that causes reduction by losing electrons; therefore, it gets oxidised.</p><p>(C) The reducing property increases from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></math> down the group. This is because the bond energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Se</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Te</mi><mo>)</mo></math> bond decreases down the group.</p><p>(D) <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8acb4ed7-eb79-4dd6-9b2c-ab78d52c34aa.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 122px;\"/> have six lone pairs</p>",
